{
 "about": "Field classes of the tools_vehicles domain for the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D tools_vehicles). 'fields' classifies, for this domain's types (house_sim/data/types/tools_vehicles.json), every property of the type data the kernel's name table misfits or does not name and every field this domain's verbs and systems write: identity = what a thing is (ratings, kinds, printed text: flow_lpm, cure_s, gauge, power_kw, stroke_l are static here, whatever the kernel's name patterns take them for); setting = what the robot sets (a car's engine and brake, clamps, an assembly's slots, a mount, inflation records, fastener_delta: the public mirror of the hidden _fasteners truth); condition = damage in its worse direction; content = what it holds or has left (a weatherstrip roll's length_m: cutting uses it up); process = transient physics and what follows from things the ledger compares (a trunk's stack height, a door's latch_ok, a drain's speed, cabin heat, wet paint, a charger's status); bookkeeping = records of what happened and mirrors of other things (layers: the loads themselves are judged; fasteners: the visible head list a close look extends; a tool's `condition` words, written when a close look shows the hidden _damage). 'types' refines a type and names what this domain writes on core things and on generic_items standing in for other domains' fixtures. 'writes': the names of 'fields' this domain writes on things of any type; the ledger applies a domain's 'fields' only to its own types, so on other types they fall back to the kernel table or the default (setting: watched, a false alarm at worst, never a hole) until the kernel reads this list (request to WP1). water_sensitive: powered tools, chargers and paper.",
